{"question_id": "V2-dev-BOOK-en-T3-002", "approach": "HYDE_6000", "approach_base": "HYDE_6000", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "K", "corpus_set": "BOOK_en", "pool_id": "BOOK-en", "answer_text": "Douglass - model: Webster's Spelling Book (Italics) and Master Thomas's copy-books\nDouglass - practice: wrote with chalk on the board fence, brick wall, and pavement; copied Italics until he could make them without looking; wrote in the spaces left in Master Thomas's copy-book, copying what he had written, until his hand was very similar to Master Thomas's\nFranklin - model: an odd volume of the Spectator (the third)\nFranklin - practice: took some of the papers, made short hints of the sentiment in each sentence, laid them by a few days, then tried to complete the papers again from the hints, and compared his version with the original to discover and correct his faults\n\nBoth used written models to imitate and then self-check: Douglass copied letters and his master's handwriting directly, while Franklin reconstructed Spectator papers from sentence hints and compared his version against the original to find and correct his faults.", "abstained": false, "evidence_items": [{"doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o012", "chars": 968, "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b120"], "cut": false}, {"doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o012", "chars": 508, "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b120"], "cut": false}, {"doc_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::o017", "chars": 605, "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::p1_b133"], "cut": false}, {"doc_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::o027", "chars": 834, "uni